Subject: [PATCH 2/2] freedreno/a3xx: retain the target format channel swap

The GMEM target channel order must match the color format for tiled
resources as well. Always use fd3_pipe2swap(), matching the resolve format,
instead of forcing WZYX when the eventual resource is tiled. With the pitch
fix alone, a BGRA upload returns red and blue interchanged when sampled.

Tested on SM-T531/Adreno305b together with patch1 using complete pixel
checks for RGBA, BGRA, A8 and L8 textures, 257x131 and 1280x800, including
unaligned overlapping partial uploads. The linear-resource path retains
its previous swap. Other GPU models/workloads remain unverified.

Base: Mesa25.0.7 plus patch1.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_gmem.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_gmem.c
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@
 
          offset = fd_resource_offset(rsc, psurf->u.tex.level,
                                      psurf->u.tex.first_layer);
-         swap = rsc->layout.tile_mode ? WZYX : fd3_pipe2swap(pformat);
+         swap = fd3_pipe2swap(pformat);
 
          if (bin_w) {
             stride = bin_w << fdl_cpp_shift(&rsc->layout);
